WEBVTT

00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:17.250
Slowly... Slowly...

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.000
What do you think I'm doing?

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.710
Thanks for helping out on your day off.

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:27.300
Yeah, I can't move another inch.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:30.970
Maybe I'll have you pay all
the rent you owe me at once.

00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.220
Okay, fine. Those who don't work...

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.770
...shall not eat.

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:42.860
I invited Oicho, too,
but she said she was busy.

00:00:42.860 --> 00:00:44.690
Ah.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:45.650
Say, Joe.

00:00:45.650 --> 00:00:46.780
Yeah?

00:00:46.780 --> 00:00:50.950
I want to interview Liu.
Anyway you can ask him for me?

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.820
He's declined interviews
with everyone else,

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.160
so this is the perfect opportunity
for a freelance guy like me.

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:57.790
Santa...

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:02.250
I know this is your job,
but sorry, I can't.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:06.840
Oh, I see. You feel sorry for him
since you're both boxers?

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:10.550
That's not it. I've already
stepped down from the ring.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:14.260
Didn't look like it from the
way you were sparring.

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.600
Even you said he looked like
the old Joe in that ring there.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:21.480
That's not what I meant...

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.900
I mean, I'd be super happy if Joe
got back into the ring, but...

00:01:52.840 --> 00:01:58.890
MEGALOBOX 2

00:03:06.200 --> 00:03:10.790
"Abuhachi's Shop"

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:16.010
I'm glad to get work,

00:03:16.010 --> 00:03:19.390
but It'd be great if it wasn't
always feast or famine.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:21.760
We didn't have much to do last month.

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.310
This is basically our
busiest time of the year.

00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.190
Thanks.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:31.400
Where'd that come from?

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.610
It's not like I have a super unique skill,

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:37.860
but I thought my craft was
going to die with me,

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:40.530
and I was fine with that.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.950
But then, you came to my shop.

00:03:45.330 --> 00:03:47.330
I've always liked fiddling
around with machines.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.460
I used to play around with
Sachio like this all the time.

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:53.380
It feel great to have someone
carry on your legacy.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.090
Then you'll pass this down
again to someone else.

00:03:56.090 --> 00:04:00.890
Though I'm an old-timer, so I won't
be able to see that for myself.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:03.260
Let's turn this back a notch.

00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:07.270
I still have a lot I need
to learn from you, Boss.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:09.650
I need you to stick around
as long as possible.

00:04:10.730 --> 00:04:13.820
And now for an update on the typhoon.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:19.820
The typhoon continues to grow even bigger
as it makes its way towards the coast.

00:04:19.820 --> 00:04:22.700
Anyone living in the warning zones
should be very cautious

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:27.000
of strong winds and rain from
late tonight into the morning.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.630
It appears that ROSCO is indeed

00:04:40.630 --> 00:04:43.550
planning to have BES get
picked up for military use.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:54.480
I apologize for asking you
to meet with me so suddenly.

00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.020
Oh, it's fine.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.570
Anytime you try to make
your dream come true,

00:04:58.570 --> 00:05:02.780
there'll always be people who try to hold
you back popping out of the woodwork.

00:05:02.780 --> 00:05:05.120
It appears that you know
what I wanted to talk about.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:10.250
If we could get data from the battlefield
that covers all the conditions,

00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:12.670
we could get this product onto
the market exponentially faster.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:15.420
We didn't decide to lend
you our technology

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:17.800
to aid your product to
expand to military use.

00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.380
You should be aware of that.

00:05:20.380 --> 00:05:25.800
I don't blame you for being hesitant
about this right now, Yukiko.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.020
But wars aren't going anywhere.

00:05:28.020 --> 00:05:32.940
So we're asking our products
be used to maintain the peace--

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:37.730
Are you suggesting that implanting a brain
chip into soldiers who've been injured

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:41.740
mentally or physically and sending them
back out to the battlefield is peaceful?

00:05:41.740 --> 00:05:44.700
I heard that is what you
proposed to the military.

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:46.870
I wouldn't say that.

00:05:46.870 --> 00:05:49.200
You're clearly trying to
make this sound malicious.

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.870
I'm sure they'd welcome the idea,

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:55.250
considering being able to reuse soldiers
would cut down on their costs greatly.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:57.250
Reuse?

00:05:57.250 --> 00:06:00.170
You're making these poor
people sound like tools.

00:06:00.170 --> 00:06:02.130
That's not like you, Yukiko.

00:06:03.260 --> 00:06:08.430
What lies at the base of this proposal
are the earnest wishes of soldiers

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.810
who have returned from the battlefield
that want to serve their nation again.

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:16.770
I want to see their wish come true.
Is that really a bad thing?

00:06:16.770 --> 00:06:21.280
So the choice will be at their own risk,
even if they die in battle?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.110
I didn't say that.

00:06:23.110 --> 00:06:27.370
But considering they don't even have
a choice now, this can give them hope.

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:32.750
Mac has lit this torch of hope for us
and I don't want to see it go out.

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:38.500
And that's why I'd like for you
to consider this as an option.

00:06:39.800 --> 00:06:44.340
Then may I see the undisclosed
data you have on Mac?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:49.260
There are claims that Mac Time is actually
abnormal behavior caused by the chip.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:54.520
It appears that Mr. Mikio Shirato has
very unfavorable opinions about BES.

00:06:54.520 --> 00:06:59.520
My brother has nothing to do with this.
We just want to investigate this closer.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.320
Wait, are you cutting us off?!

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:03.400
No.

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:06.450
We need to be as careful as possible
to get this product out there

00:07:06.450 --> 00:07:09.280
and we need to think about Mac's health.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:13.160
Yikes... You almost
gave me a heart attack.

00:07:18.290 --> 00:07:21.300
I'll send you the data
as soon as I get back.

00:07:21.300 --> 00:07:22.630
Thank you.

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:33.390
I hope you'll keep your reports as
neutral as possible, Ms. Asamoto.

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:42.070
Ma'am.

00:07:42.070 --> 00:07:47.740
Cutting ties with ROSCO will cause
a huge financial loss to our company.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:52.330
I cannot make any rash decisions.

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:55.000
Even if decision will go against ideals.

00:07:59.630 --> 00:08:02.000
His exam seems to have gone well.

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.760
They were saying he might be able
to start PT quicker than expected.

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:08.010
I see.

00:08:08.010 --> 00:08:12.300
Liu will be all right.
He'll get through this.

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:16.520
You can't blame yourself for this, Yuri.

00:08:16.520 --> 00:08:17.980
Ever since he woke up,

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:24.150
he hasn't expressed any doubt
or said a single complaint.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:27.570
He's always dreamed about having
a match like Joe and I had...

00:08:27.570 --> 00:08:29.700
...but his career as a
boxer's been snuffed out

00:08:29.700 --> 00:08:32.370
before he could even
reach his true potential.

00:08:35.410 --> 00:08:39.000
When I woke up, I heard them say

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:43.130
that some of the paralysis
would remain even after I did PT.

00:08:43.130 --> 00:08:46.090
I cried like a madman all night.

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:48.130
I mean, it's not fair, right?

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:52.140
They're seriously trying to take
Megalo-boxing away from me.

00:08:52.140 --> 00:08:53.890
Any chance you'll fully recover?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:57.350
Nope. The docs seemed
pretty certain about that.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.440
But I haven't given up.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:06.070
Thinking that some kid off the streets
like me could ever become champion

00:09:06.070 --> 00:09:09.990
was just a dream that
only Yuri and I shared.

00:09:09.990 --> 00:09:14.410
And I'm pretty sure that even
Yuri would be against this,

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:16.580
so now I'm the only dreamer left.

00:09:16.580 --> 00:09:22.580
And that's fine. I'm never going to
give up on this dream or myself.

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:26.590
Otherwise, I'm going to
end up hating myself.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.380
I'll believe in you, too.

00:09:30.380 --> 00:09:35.220
So, yeah... We're gonna have to
postpone our match for a while.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:36.430
Sure.

00:09:42.940 --> 00:09:45.480
You're making me rich, Sachio.

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:48.690
Damn it, don't win the
one time I didn't bet on you!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.490
You better win again next time.

00:09:56.620 --> 00:09:59.370
I told you I don't want that.

00:09:59.370 --> 00:10:01.710
I thought you might've changed your mind.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:05.170
You and Abuhachi need to
mind your own business.

00:10:05.170 --> 00:10:07.630
I'm not leaving the ring.

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:11.840
Have you gone back to the gym lately?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.590
Looks like Joe's adamant
about restoring the place.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:19.810
At first, I thought he was
just messing around,

00:10:19.810 --> 00:10:22.100
but I guess I was wrong.

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:26.610
Lately, Santa and Bonjiri have
been helping him out, too.

00:10:26.610 --> 00:10:29.360
He's just looking for forgiveness.

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.900
I'm not about to give him
the attention he's asking for.

00:10:35.660 --> 00:10:37.370
You might be right.

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:41.540
But seeing him made me remember

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:43.490
D21 Engineering Support Association

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.460
that you're the only one who can
make decisions for yourself.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:49.130
You should do what you truly want.

00:10:52.970 --> 00:10:54.430
I am.

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:21.330
No point coming by now.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:26.500
I should've been there
for you more back then.

00:11:28.250 --> 00:11:32.590
I was scared. I couldn't bear
all that weight on my own

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:35.170
and I didn't know what to do.

00:11:35.170 --> 00:11:37.340
I tried to figure out what I
could do for you guys and--

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.510
Don't give me any of
your pathetic excuses!

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.060
You're the one who destroyed everything!

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:49.270
You really thought everything would go
back to normal if you rebuilt the gym?

00:11:49.270 --> 00:11:52.110
Gym Nowhere died a long time ago!

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:07.120
All I want to do...

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:11.460
...is see the lights go on
in that place once again.

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:20.890
Pops!

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:24.810
It's all right. It'll stop soon.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:29.190
Don't you dare tell Joe.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:32.150
He's not as confident as you think.

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:35.400
I don't want him gettin'
anxious before the match.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:38.530
You're so selfish. Both you and Joe.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:39.780
Yeah.

00:12:39.780 --> 00:12:44.280
We ended up taking that match
without talking to you runts first.

00:12:44.280 --> 00:12:48.250
If you just told Joe to stop, he'd...

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:52.580
We had always put everything
on the line for his dream.

00:12:52.580 --> 00:12:54.920
That's how we became a family.

00:12:57.090 --> 00:13:00.720
He's scared that the lights
are gonna go out.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:02.090
The lights?

00:13:02.090 --> 00:13:06.810
The lights we always
believed in back home.

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:12.150
He really thinks they're gonna
go out when I'm gone.

00:13:12.150 --> 00:13:17.110
He's just like you. He wants to do
nothing more than protect all of you.

00:13:18.610 --> 00:13:21.990
I don't understand any of that.

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.840
Mommy, is here okay?

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.510
Yes, thank you.

00:13:51.940 --> 00:13:55.310
Daddy's rewatching the same part again.

00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.190
You've gotta do a lot of research when you
want to take down a strong opponent.

00:14:02.070 --> 00:14:04.660
You look so scary here. I don't like it.

00:14:08.120 --> 00:14:10.580
All right, time for bed.

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:11.790
Can you read this to me first?

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:21.130
"The Hummingbird and the Nomad"

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.580
Miguel, Daddy's tired, so it'll
have to wait until tomorrow.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:21.050
It's fine. Just don't fall asleep
before I'm done like last time.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:28.680
As the wind whirled by,

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.310
a hummingbird appeared before the nomad

00:14:31.310 --> 00:14:34.390
as they made their way
through the wasteland.

00:14:34.390 --> 00:14:38.940
"Will you listen to my song, Nomad?"

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:42.860
"I'm in a hurry. Ask someone else."

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:47.910
But the hummingbird just wouldn't
give up and pursued the nomad.

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:52.200
"Please. I must sing my song."

00:14:52.200 --> 00:14:56.880
"You're rather selfish.
Sorry, but I'm just not in the mood."

00:14:56.880 --> 00:15:00.800
"I'm on a journey to die."

00:15:04.170 --> 00:15:10.100
"But that's ridiculous.
Who goes on a journey to die?"

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:14.690
"It's the truth. Why would I
bother lying before I die?"

00:15:14.690 --> 00:15:17.770
But the hummingbird refused to give up.

00:15:17.770 --> 00:15:19.980
"Then how about this?"

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:25.820
"If I can make you lie,
listen to my song."

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:30.200
"If I fail to do so, I will say no more."

00:15:30.200 --> 00:15:34.660
Wanting to be freed from
the persistent pest,

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:39.000
the nomad agreed.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.170
Joe!

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:43.380
"Why do you want to die?"

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:47.090
"Because I lost everything."

00:15:47.090 --> 00:15:48.640
"That's a lie."

00:15:48.640 --> 00:15:50.890
"But it's not a lie."

00:15:50.890 --> 00:15:55.730
"I lost my home, my fortune...
and my family died from illness."

00:15:55.730 --> 00:15:58.310
"I've got nothing left."

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:01.650
Joe! We can't!

00:16:07.910 --> 00:16:14.330
"No. You still have eyes to see me
and ears to hear my song."

00:16:14.330 --> 00:16:18.000
"You even have a mouth to speak to me."

00:16:19.120 --> 00:16:22.420
"Yes, you're right."

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:25.380
Though they felt that
they had been duped,

00:16:25.380 --> 00:16:28.010
the nomad admitted defeat.

00:16:32.850 --> 00:16:35.430
Thanks, Oicho.

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:38.560
This place is precious to me, too.

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:41.650
Sachio never did come.

00:16:41.650 --> 00:16:43.730
He's probably tired from his match.

00:16:43.730 --> 00:16:46.240
He should just quit.

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:49.240
At this rate he's just
gonna be a junk boxer.

00:16:49.240 --> 00:16:52.120
He's apparently fine with how things are.

00:16:52.120 --> 00:16:54.030
When he was little,

00:16:54.030 --> 00:16:55.870
he said he wanted to become an engineer.

00:16:55.870 --> 00:17:00.330
Yeah, he said he wanted to
do the same job Pops had.

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:05.420
He and Oicho would go help
out Abuhachi all the time.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:07.550
Until we lost this place, that is.

00:17:07.550 --> 00:17:10.840
We were pretty busy back then.

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:15.010
We had no idea he was
practicing Megalo-boxing.

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:19.690
But whenever we'd run into him,
he seemed different.

00:17:19.690 --> 00:17:22.060
Abuhachi was worried about him,

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:27.230
so he had an engineer buddy write
him up a letter of recommendation,

00:17:27.230 --> 00:17:30.030
but the kid refuses to take it.

00:17:30.030 --> 00:17:34.070
Boss and Mr. Aragaki are
always looking after us.

00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:38.200
Why does Sachio insist
on getting into that ring?

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:39.910
He wanted to protect this place.

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:54.430
"Team Nowhere"

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:46.340
After you left, Sachio was the
one supporting this place.

00:17:46.340 --> 00:17:50.300
If we can get this place back up,
everyone would come back.

00:17:50.300 --> 00:17:54.430
We'd all be able to live together again,
just like when Pops was alive.

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:59.680
It may not seem like it, but he felt
responsible for driving you away.

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:03.600
He was scared to lose
any more of his family.

00:18:06.150 --> 00:18:10.780
That's why Sachio did everything
he could to take your place.

00:18:22.620 --> 00:18:26.590
He's trying to close the way to the
future with such trivial morality.

00:18:26.590 --> 00:18:30.670
Are siblings destined
to think like each other?

00:18:30.670 --> 00:18:34.300
That is possible if their
moral values are the same,

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:36.140
but I'm not sure if--

00:18:36.140 --> 00:18:38.680
Lighten up, will you?

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:40.350
I was kidding.

00:18:40.350 --> 00:18:41.930
I'm terribly sorry, sir.

00:18:43.230 --> 00:18:48.820
Anyway, If this thesis spreads,
Mac's product value will go down.

00:18:44.180 --> 00:18:51.440
"ROSCO's Brain Chip's Abnormal Behavior"
"Warnings About Its Practical Application"

00:18:48.820 --> 00:18:51.360
And so will ROSCO's stock.

00:18:51.440 --> 00:19:00.200
"Gear Technology Research /
Professor Mikio Shirato"

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.860
He's a professor at
your university, isn't he?

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:57.740
Do you know how many
donations we've made there?

00:18:57.740 --> 00:19:00.120
Talk about being stabbed in the back.

00:19:00.540 --> 00:19:02.450
As the head of the
developmental department,

00:19:02.450 --> 00:19:06.420
I need you to show him who's boss.

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.040
Of course. If you insist.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:10.250
Oh, yeah.

00:19:11.550 --> 00:19:16.510
Send Shirato Mac's undisclosed data.

00:19:16.510 --> 00:19:18.850
Just make the usual tweaks.

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:21.310
Please excuse me.

00:19:26.980 --> 00:19:30.650
Looks like we're going to have
to make the first move.

00:19:37.280 --> 00:19:41.120
So how long haven't you
been able to sleep?

00:19:41.120 --> 00:19:43.790
It's not every day.

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:47.500
Lately, it's just been after my matches.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:50.630
My memory seems fuzzier than usual.

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:54.630
Honestly, I barely even
remember my last match.

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:57.470
Well, of course you'd be nervous.

00:19:57.470 --> 00:20:00.010
You pulled off a victory of a lifetime.

00:20:01.390 --> 00:20:03.680
I'm scared of myself.

00:20:03.680 --> 00:20:05.230
I'm scared that I'm going to

00:20:05.230 --> 00:20:08.350
do that again to someone in
the ring without realizing it.

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:12.400
But you just became the champ.
Your career's just begun.

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:18.660
The reason I came back to the ring is
I wanted my son to see me up there.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:21.700
I didn't need anything else.

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:26.410
So I'm not sure if I have a
reason to fight anymore.

00:20:32.340 --> 00:20:36.800
When I asked you if you wanted
to get back into that ring,

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:39.380
I asked you why you retired, didn't I?

00:20:39.380 --> 00:20:40.260
Yes.

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.970
And this is what you said...

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.980
That the way that "Gearless" Joe
challenged the champion Yuri

00:20:47.980 --> 00:20:52.650
at the finals of the first
Megalonia was everything.

00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.940
After seeing how much
Joe shined in that ring,

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:59.360
you realized he was the real deal.

00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:04.990
It wasn't jealousy.
He just moved you that much.

00:21:04.990 --> 00:21:11.830
He made you finally realize just how
unfit you were to be in that ring.

00:21:11.830 --> 00:21:18.130
If I hadn't seen that match,
I might've kept dragging my feet.

00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.010
You still haven't figured it out?

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:25.430
You're currently in the exact
position Joe was in back then.

00:21:28.890 --> 00:21:32.650
Come on. Let's dream together again.

00:21:52.750 --> 00:21:56.210
"All right, I lose."

00:21:56.210 --> 00:21:59.510
The nomad didn't want any more trouble

00:21:59.510 --> 00:22:04.430
and stopped to hear the
hummingbird's song.

00:22:04.430 --> 00:22:07.260
The voice was so beautiful,

00:22:07.260 --> 00:22:14.730
that it filled the nomad's empty heart
with a gentle warmth just for a moment.

00:22:18.230 --> 00:22:20.820
After it had finished its song,

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:23.240
the hummingbird flew
towards the ray of sunlight

00:22:23.240 --> 00:22:26.080
that was peeking through the clouds.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:32.030
"Affordable Chinese Food Ichibanya"

00:22:32.030 --> 00:22:38.960
"Mac Challenges the Legend
For His Next Match!!
Does This Mean a Comeback for 'Gearless' Joe?!"
